# README criterion 5 (agent-exchange-2026-08 P12 G4): "An artifact that
# names a digest it does not carry is refused at `a2a validate`, locally,
# before any pull request." The readiness audit found the wiring from
# `a2a validate` to internal/validate's REF-017 check (checkPossession,
# possession.go) real by reading source, but no exec'd-binary run had ever
# asserted the refusal — this scenario is that run.
#
# Two artifacts, byte-identical except for one line, so the refusal is
# provably caused by the undeclared `sha256:` token and not by anything else
# in the fixture (e.g. a coincidentally-invalid needed_by or a stray schema
# violation): digest-not-carried.md names a digest with no matching
# attachments[].digest and is refused; digest-absent.md drops that one line
# and is valid. Both frontmatter blocks are the internal/validate package's
# own possession_test.go incident reconstruction
# (docs/inbox/agent-exchange-review/03-bytes-note.md), adapted to this
# harness's fixture-space/axon/beta participants.
mkdir .a2a/staging
cp digest-not-carried.md .a2a/staging/digest-not-carried.md
! exec a2a validate --all
stdout 'REF-017'
rm .a2a/staging/digest-not-carried.md

cp digest-absent.md .a2a/staging/digest-absent.md
exec a2a validate --all
stdout '"valid": true'

